# Minimal patches applied to vendored upstream files after copy (see Makefile regen).
#
# 0001-exception-ptr-versioned-namespace.patch
#   Puts std::exception_ptr and the current/rethrow/uncaught_exceptions operations +
#   nested_exception into the VERSIONED ABI namespace (std::__sprt) instead of the
#   canonical std that libc++'s _LIBCPP_BEGIN_UNVERSIONED_NAMESPACE_STD gives them.
#   Rationale: sprt OWNS its libc++ tree and provides these out of line itself
#   (libc_wrapper/cxx/SPRTCxxException.cpp, in std::__sprt); leaving them canonical
#   makes vendored TUs (e.g. src/libcxx/future.cpp) reference a bare std::exception_ptr
#   that clashes with a foreign/system libc++'s canonical symbols on the ABI-shared
#   targets (macOS) -- the same reason libstdc++ hides them in std::__exception_ptr.
#   std::terminate / std::set_terminate / std::type_info stay canonical (libc++abi owns
#   them). See runtime/libcxx/libcxx.mk and the SPRTCxx threading/future TUs.

# 0002-runtime-owned-std-symbols-versioned.patch
#   Full canonical-namespace isolation: every symbol the SPRT RUNTIME defines moves to
#   the versioned namespace (std::__sprt); only libc++abi remains a canonical-std
#   provider (its job — the platform C++ ABI layer: std::exception hierarchy,
#   type_info, terminate, new_handler, ...).
#   - <stdexcept>: the nine exception classes (upstream: "purposefully not using
#     versioning namespace") -> versioned; their out-of-line members come from
#     src/SPRTCxxStdexcept.cpp (also versioned).
#   - <optional>/<variant>/<any>: bad_optional_access / bad_variant_access /
#     bad_any_cast -> versioned (same TU defines them).
#   - <__new/exceptions.h>: only __throw_bad_alloc -> versioned (bad_alloc & co stay
#     canonical: libc++abi provides them).
#   - <__new/nothrow_t.h>: only the `nothrow` OBJECT -> versioned; the nothrow_t TYPE
#     stays canonical (it participates in the replaceable operator new/delete
#     manglings, which must match libc++abi's weak set).
#   - src/new_helpers.cpp: the nothrow/__throw_bad_alloc definitions follow.
#   Companion (non-vendored) changes: sprt/cxx/compare and sprt/cxx/__new/nothrow.h
#   hand-written branches use __SPRT_STD_OWNED_* (inline __sprt on system-ABI
#   targets) for the strong/weak/partial_ordering constants and the nothrow object;
#   runtime_core_defaults.cpp defines std::nothrow versioned accordingly.

# 0003-sprt-suppress-win32api.patch
#   Lets the sprt overlay turn OFF _LIBCPP_WIN32API on the *-windows-msvc target. __config
#   auto-defines it from _WIN32, which switches every OS-service subsystem of libc++ to its
#   <windows.h> backend: the filesystem reimplements stat/statvfs/readlink/... against WinAPI
#   in src/libcxx/filesystem/posix_compat.h, chrono/system_error/ostream-print take their
#   Win32 paths, and path::value_type becomes wchar_t. sprt already ships a full POSIX libc on
#   Windows (char/UTF-8 stat, statvfs, open, clock_gettime, strerror, fopen — each converts to
#   WinAPI internally), so those reimplementations only duplicate sprt's libc and risk
#   diverging from it (e.g. two statvfs). The patch gates `#define _LIBCPP_WIN32API` (and the
#   _wfopen wchar-open path via _LIBCPP_HAS_OPEN_WITH_WCHAR) on `!defined(_LIBCPP_SPRT_NO_WIN32API)`,
#   a macro the overlay sets in <__config_site> for _WIN32. The whole library then takes its
#   POSIX code paths and routes through sprt: path is char/UTF-8 and files open via char fopen.
#   _LIBCPP_SHORT_WCHAR / _LIBCPP_MSVCRT[_LIKE] are deliberately left as __config sets them —
#   they describe the compiler's 16-bit wchar_t ABI and the C-runtime/locale-backend flavor,
#   not the OS API surface. Companion (non-vendored) change: the _LIBCPP_SPRT_NO_WIN32API
#   define lives in include_libc/cxx/__config_site (the overlay, not a vendored mirror).
